ce the \\(k\\) sunny lines given by Lemma 4 (for \\(k\\) odd).  \n\n   All lines are distinct, every point of \\(S_n\\) lies on at least one of them, and exactly \\(k\\) of the lines are sunny.\n\n   Hence the set of admissible values of \\(k\\) is precisely  \n\n   \\[\n   \\boxed{\\{\\,0\\,\\}\\cup\\{\\,k\\in\\mathbb Z_{\\ge0}\\mid k\\text{ is odd and }k\\le n\\,\\}} .\n   \\]\n\n   In particular, a covering with all \\(n\\) lines sunny exists exactly when \\(n\\) itself is odd.  \n\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\text{For every }n\\ge3,\\;k=0\\text{ or }k\\text{ odd }(1\\le k\\le n)\\text{ are precisely the possible numbers of sunny lines}.}\n\\]\n\n\n### Verification Task Reminder ###\n\nYour task is to act as an IMO grader. Now, generate the **summary** and the **step-by-step verification log** for the solution above. In your log, justify each correct step and explain in detail any errors or justification gaps you find, as specified in the instructions above.\n\n"
